Entries for the Quebec QSO Party used by in-province (VE2) stations
The 17 administrative regions (each its own multiplier), then the 50 US states and DC, the Canadian provinces and territories but Quebec, and one DX
The rules - a VE2 station is given one multiplier point for each first contact with a province or Canadian territory, US state or DX
The rules - Hawaii HI, Alaska AK and District of Columbia DC shall be included in the continental states (S51.DOM holds the 48, AK, HI and DC)
Quebec is not a multiplier - the Province of Quebec QC is not a valid territory entry - so P12/P13 are NOT included
P12/P13 also give Quebec the alias QUE, which is the Capitale-Nationale region code, and VE2, which would make the rover strip take W2ABC/VE2 as a region
Newfoundland NF and Labrador LB are TWO multipliers in the rules Appendix II (NY4I, GitHub 128), so they are written here, not taken from P13 (one Nl)
NT and NWT are one territory listed twice by the rules, so one multiplier (NY4I, GitHub 128)
Other DXCC entities must be logged as DX - one DX multiplier, per band
The region file comes FIRST so a region code always wins
No line of this header may hold an equals sign - the reader takes any such line as an entry
https://quebecqsoparty.org/rules-quebec-qso-party/

INCLUDE FILE quebec_cty.dom
INCLUDE FILE S51.DOM
Nf = NF,^Newfoundland
Lb = LB,^Labrador
Pe = PE,^Prince Edward Island
Nb = NB,^New Brunswick
Ns = NS,^Nova Scotia
On = ON,^Ontario
Mb = MB,^Manitoba
Sk = SK,^Saskatchewan
Ab = AB,^Alberta
Bc = BC,^British Columbia
Nt = NT,NWT,^Northwest Territories
Yt = YT,^Yukon
Nu = NU,^Nunavut
Dx = DX
